---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CliSurface from '../components/CliSurface.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Features"
  description="Everything postiee ships, and everything it deliberately does not — with the reason for each omission."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Scope</p>
  <h1>Features</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    postiee does a small number of things and does them properly. The list of
    what it will never do is longer than the list of what it will, and that is
    deliberate.
  </p>

  <h2>What ships</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Command</th>
        <th scope="col">What it does</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>post</code></td>
        <td>
          Create a post. Text, one image with alt text, or a body read from a
          file. Visibility is <code>PUBLIC</code>, <code>CONNECTIONS</code>, or
          <code>LOGGED_IN</code>.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>history</code></td>
        <td>Every post recorded locally, newest first.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>search</code></td>
        <td>
          Full-text search over your own post bodies. Porter stemming, ANDed
          terms, and arbitrary junk input handled without erroring.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>forget</code></td>
        <td>Remove a post from your local history.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>auth</code></td>
        <td>OAuth login, logout, and status. Credentials read from a file, not
        from flags.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>doctor</code></td>
        <td>Config, credential, and API reachability check.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>--agent</code></td>
        <td>
          Global flag adding <code>--json --compact --no-input --no-color</code>
          for machine-readable output.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>What deliberately does not ship</h2>

  <figure>
    <CliSurface />
    <figcaption>
      Every omitted command, with the reason it is not "unimplemented" but
      unimplementable.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Capability</th>
        <th scope="col">Status</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Comments</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge mid">partner approval</span> Needs the Community
          Management API.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Reactions and likes</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge mid">partner approval</span> Same.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Analytics — impressions, followers, profile views</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge mid">partner approval</span> Separate member
          analytics scopes.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Reading your own posts back</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge no">closed</span>
          <code>r_member_social</code> is not accepting requests at this time.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Reading who reacted to a post</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge no">closed</span> Reaction identities are never
          returned to a member app at any tier.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Messaging and DMs</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge no">no API exists</span> No product in the
          catalogue, no endpoint in the docs, and mass messaging is an explicit
          prohibited use.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Connection invitations</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge no">no API exists</span> Same.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Looking up another member's profile</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge no">no API exists</span> Person IDs are app-scoped,
          so there is no way to resolve someone else's ID.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Scheduled posts</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge mid">client-side only</span> There is no
          <code>publishAt</code> field anywhere in LinkedIn's post schema.
          Scheduling means a local timer.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Multi-image and video posts</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge mid">partner approval</span> Single image works
          self-serve; the rest do not.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Why so many omissions</h2>

  <p>
    LinkedIn's API is not designed for individuals posting to their own feed. It
    is designed for marketing platforms managing thousands of pages, so the
    surface that suits you — read your posts, react to them, see how they did —
    is exactly the surface that requires becoming a vetted partner.
  </p>
  <p>
    Shipping stubs for those would be worse than silence. A <code>comment</code>
    command that returns 403 on first use teaches the user nothing and wastes
    their time; an absent command tells them the truth immediately. So the
    tool ships only what genuinely works, and the docs say plainly why the rest
    is out of reach.
  </p>

  <h2>Quality guarantees</h2>

  <p>
    Every number in the README and every behaviour described above is produced by
    a test, not asserted by hand.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Property</th>
        <th scope="col">Status</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Porter stemming — <code>authentic</code> finds
          <code>authentication</code></td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Multi-term AND narrows rather than widens</td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>An absent term returns nothing</td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Junk input never errors — <code>"</code>, <code>AND</code>,
          <code>()</code>, <code>NEAR(a b)</code>, <code>--</code></td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Re-recording a post upserts instead of duplicating</td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Deleting removes the search index entry too</td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Post ID read from the response header, not the body</td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Image upload performs exactly two calls</td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>URNs in paths are fully percent-encoded</td>
        <td><span class="badge ok">pass</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Partial-word prefix search</td>
        <td>
          <span class="badge mid">not supported</span> FTS5 indexes whole
          tokens. Documented rather than papered over.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</Base>